# Zatroz — server and data

Use when touching `src/server`, API routes, env access, enquiries, email, or databases.

- Keep credentials and secrets **server-only** (no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for secrets). Prefer helpers under `src/server/`.
- Validate at the **server boundary** even if the browser already validated.
- Enquiry records must **not** be publicly readable; content-editor roles do **not** include enquiry access by default.
- Application database is **MongoDB Atlas** (not Supabase). Keep DB calls in narrow server repositories; never spread request JSON into queries.
- Staff admin auth (Better Auth) and media binaries (Cloudinary) are planned in A02/A04 — do not invent homemade sessions or unrestricted URL fetchers.
- Do **not** log PII (names, emails, message bodies) in plain application logs or analytics.
- Report success to the visitor only after a **durable save**; notification failure must be recoverable with bounded retries.
- When integrations exist: keep test/preview data and recipients separate from production.
- Do not invent live integrations. Follow planning in `docs/planning/01-project-scope.md` and later env docs.
